z3 4.3.1 bug: when a string literal contains an invalid escape sequence (e.g. "\d"), z3 reports the error but then treats the following close-quote as an escaped quote, consuming all subsequent input as part of the unterminated string. This causes a deadlock because jSMTLIB sends the next command but z3 never responds. Needs investigation: either validate string escapes before sending to z3, or detect the deadlock.
